, "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1b, is a modification of the a 2 / o method to increase the removal efficiency of phosphorus and nitrogen, wastewater through the first settling tank 100 anaerobic reactor 200, the first anoxic reactor 300, the first aerobic oxidation tank 400, the second anoxic reactor 500, the second aerobic reactor 600 and the second precipitation tank 700, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100387324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by desorption of the biofilm attached to the membrane, it prevents anaerobic conditions due to (increase) clogging of the filtration pores and provides a growth environment for microorganisms attached to the suspension contact media, and also provides direct filtration in the oxidation tank without the need for a separate precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a highly concentrated precipitation tank for filtration, oxidation, and decomposition to remove biochemical oxygen demand (bod) and suspended solids (ss)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100440250-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after adjusting the ph, the oxidation reaction is carried out in the reactor, and then, the precipitate is adjusted by adjusting the appropriate ph in the precipitation tank for aggregation and precipitation, and then neutralized so as not to affect the microbial growth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442932-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the secondary treatment water in which the solid matter is removed by switching to the secondary precipitation tank 12b is sent to the oxidation tank 22, and the sludge precipitated in the secondary precipitation tank 12b is for the primary sludge treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the precipitation in the settling tank (l2a, b) to the decoloration treatment by the electrolytic oxidation treatment and untreated to remove the organic pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "after the oxidation treatment, it is sent to the reaction tank 18 to supply the emulsion resin and the flocculant to solidify the unremoved heavy metal component, and then to stir slowly by the flocculation tank stirrer 21 to facilitate precipitation or pressure flotation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100518722-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the culture medium is supplied to the secondary aeration tank 16 while (increase) the culture medium circulates through the magnetic field of the magnet by the pump 32, and the blue water, which is fed to the upper portion of the secondary precipitation tank 17, is sent to the oxidation tank 20 to peroxide"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100624556-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a third purification step in which the inflow water, which has passed the precipitation step, is biologically purified while (increase) being introduced and passed through the contact oxidation tank in which the microbial contact material is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the agglomeration tank and the belt press may be further mounted between the ozone treatment tank and the ultraviolet treatment tank, thereby further improving the filtration efficiency by further performing the removal of agglomerates through oxidation and precipitation and aggregation by the oxidant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100712175-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "organic matter in the microbial catalyst oxidation tank plays an important role for the formation of the floc, when the lack of organic matter in the floc weakens the floc strength may be poor sludge precipitation due to (increase) pin floc (clock) or floc release phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100969208-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3, a sedimentation tank, a primary contact aeration tank, a precipitation tank, a secondary contact aeration tank, and a sludge-reduce (increase)d soil-coated contact oxidation sewage treatment reactor, the upper part of each treatment tank, which was a contact filtration tank and a discharge tank, was covered with porous soil in which grass was planted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, after stopping the compressor 610 to induce (increase) precipitation of the oxidation catalyst particles 320, the concentrated water is transferred to the concentrated water treatment tank 430 via the concentrated water valve 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the aging reaction of the oxide of the aeration oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank 100, and precipitates the precipitate produced it is preferable that a reaction precipitation tank 200 for performing the precipitation step is provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050144-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, biological treatment apparatus for sewage and wastewater, which is widely used at present, is provided with an aeration tank, which is an organic oxidation tank, and a precipitation tank for precipitating microorganisms grown in the aeration tank, thereby oxidizing and removing organic matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "US-10696574-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in step (1), after the oxidation reaction and the precipitation reaction, the precipitation can be removed by any suitable method in the art, such as filtering, and the employed filtering apparatus can be any filtering apparatus known in the art, preferably sedimentation tank, sand filter, multi-media filter, etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this system thus allows the sulphur to oxidize and precipitate in the aeration/precipitation tank and the iron to continue its oxidation and precipitation in such aeration/precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, after stopping the compressor 610 to induce precipitation of the oxidation catalyst particles 320, the concentrated water is transferred to the concentrated water treatment tank 430 via the concentrated water valve 420"}]</data>
</edge>
