  <data key="d5">["pipe", "flow", "platinum", "process", "resin", "evaporation", "system", "build", "ion", "recovery", "up", "action", "exchanger", "result", "rate", "sensor", "apparatus", "particle", "settling", "pump", "water", "wastewater", "claim", "efficiency", "way", "response", "addition", "fouling", "start", "heat", "scaling", "deposit", "solid", "side", "processing", "chamber", "waste", "input", "part", "tank", "initio", "feed", "transfer", "additive", "example", "biofouling", "wall", "steam", "exchange", "clogging", "sediment", "tube", "filter", "change", "ab", "fluid", "surface", "stream"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["flow", "accord", "prevent", "contact", "take", "eliminate", "pretreate", "foul", "call", "configure", "monitor", "suspend", "start", "locate", "detect", "control", "deposit", "remove", "produce", "cool", "reduce", "be", "change", "build up", "undergo", "pass"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10118835-B2", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "typically, input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-10376807-B2", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "typically, input water is pretreated to prevent clogging and fouling of the evaporation chambers due to settling of the sediment inherent in the input water stream as well as to reduce the scaling of the chamber walls"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3685113-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, fouling deposited on the surfaces of the heat exchanger contacted by the process steam can reduce (remove) thermal transfer to the cooling water stream"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3685113-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "likewise, fouling deposited on the surfaces of the heat exchanger contacted by the cooling water stream can also reduce (remove) the thermal transfer to the cooling water stream"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3685113-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (remove), fouling build-up on the process stream side of the heat exchanger may be significantly greater than on the cooling water stream side of the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3685113-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by monitoring (remove) the rate at which fouling builds up on the heat exchanger and the corresponding rate at which the thermal efficiency changes for the heat exchanger, interventional action may be taken on the cooling water side by controlling pump 106 to control the addition of one or more chemical additives to the cooling water stream in response to detecting changes in thermal efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3707457-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "by monitoring (remove) the rate at which fouling builds up on the heat exchanger and the corresponding rate at which the thermal efficiency changes for the heat exchanger, interventional action may be taken on the cooling water side by controlling pump 106 to control the addition of one or more chemical additives to the cooling water stream in response to detecting changes in thermal efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3976536-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "process according to any of the previous claims, wherein the waste water stream is passed through the heat exchanger with the particles from the start of the process to remove the fouling on the surface of the tubes as it starts to build up"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3976536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the waste water stream is passed through the heat exchanger with the particles from the start of the process to remove the fouling on the surface of the tubes ab initio, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-5736059-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "changing the laminar flow of a wastewater stream into turbulent flow, would reduce (remove) or eliminate fouling in the lower wastewater heat recovery apparatus heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-8741100-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "feed streams that produce deposits on heat exchangers while (remove) undergoing processing are called fouling fluids"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3685113-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by monitoring the rate at which fouling builds up on the heat exchanger and the corresponding rate at which the thermal efficiency changes for the heat exchanger, interventional action may be taken on the cooling water side by controlling pump 106 to control the addition of one or more chemical additives to the cooling water stream in response to detecting changes in thermal efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3707457-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "by monitoring the rate at which fouling builds up on the heat exchanger and the corresponding rate at which the thermal efficiency changes for the heat exchanger, interventional action may be taken on the cooling water side by controlling pump 106 to control the addition of one or more chemical additives to the cooling water stream in response to detecting changes in thermal efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "US-8097212-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the simplest way to prevent biofouling of the platinum redox sensor is to locate it in a strongly flowing part of the water stream in the pipe, e.g., away from the walls"}, {"pat_id": "US-8425768-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "mechanical filter 412 may be configured to remove suspended solids and other particles to prevent clogging or fouling of ion exchange (i.e., resin) tanks 402 downstream in system 400"}]</data>
</edge>
