  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent the wear of the member due to the high speed flow, a filter (not shown) for trapping sand or the like between the inlet port 403 and the upstream side supply valve v1u on the downstream side of the pump p is appropriately used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, due to excessive wear height and river water backflow, the domestic sewer pipeline system is over-planned in the upstream pipeline, so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, due to excessive wear height and river water backflow, the domestic sewer pipeline system is over-planned in the upstream pipeline, so there is no contradiction in the downstream pipeline where all sewage and rainfall runoff are discharged to the river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent the wear of the member due to (affect) the high speed flow, a filter (not shown) for trapping sand or the like between the inlet port 403 and the upstream side supply valve v1u on the downstream side of the pump p is appropriately used"}, {"pat_id": "US-8262752-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another illustrative, non-exclusive example, frequent and sudden starting and stopping of the flow of feed stream 16 from the feedstock delivery system may affect components of the feedstock delivery system, such as by causing wear on a pump and/or drive system therefor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11951424-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these types of strainer systems are prone to failure due to the particles in the feed stream interfering with the free movement of the system due to mechanical wear or jamming and ultimately failure of the cleaning mechanism"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by maintaining the adsorbent material in the biological reactor 202 or other upstream of the membrane operating system 204, the suspended-media membrane biological reactor system minimizes the possibility of contamination and / or wear of the membrane operating system tank membrane by the adsorbent material, remove"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent the wear of the member due to the high speed flow, a filter (not shown) for trapping sand or the like between the inlet port 403 and the upstream side supply valve v1u on the downstream side of the pump p is appropriately used"}]</data>
