o range in winter, rupture due to (thereby) freezing in valves or pipes may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent (thereby) freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, in the case of a water valve located outdoors, it is difficult to use the water pipe or the tap water inside the water valve due to (thereby) the freezing temperature in winter, and the volume expansion of the frozen tap water causes the water pipe or the connection parts of the water pipe to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in order to prevent (thereby) freezing of tap water, conventionally, a method of warming the water valve and the water pipe by wrapping the surroundings of the water valve and the water pipe with a heat insulating material has been most widely used, but the effect is insufficient when the temperature drops significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the automatic dripping device 100 for freezing prevent (thereby)ion according to the present embodiment may open and close the on/off valve 140 by a specific angle according to the temperature data obtained from the temperature detector 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the power supply unit 170 may provide power stored therein to the temperature detection unit 120, the control unit 130, and the opening/closing valve driving unit when the power supplied from the outside to the automatic dripping device 100 for prevent (thereby)ing freezing is cut off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to (thereby) low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, it is possible to prevent (thereby) freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44, solar cell 55, temperature sensor, signal transmitter, and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore, when the temperature drops, such as in the winter, freezing due to (thereby) residual water inside the flow path is inevitable, and when freezing occurs, the entire water angle valve must be replaced, which inevitably results in excessive costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to solve the above problems, a heating freeze protection device has been proposed, which installs a separate heater around the valve and the pipe to prevent (thereby) freezing by heating the pipe when the ambient temperature drops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe (p2), when the temperature is less than the set temperature, the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent (thereby) freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the flow sensor to prevent (thereby) the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor (5) located in the water pipe (p2) below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the system may receive (thereby) weather data, and if there is prediction of sub-zero temperatures in the forecast, the sys