coming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this heat exchanger interface will help in keeping the temperature of the fluid in the modified inlet block 444 constant during the pressure decay, thereby improving the accuracy of the rate-of-decay measurement by avoiding fluctuations in the rate that may have otherwise been cause by (thus) fluctuations in the temperature of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050727-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the outer mixing part 2 formed as described above slides in contact with the inner diameter or one side and blocks and opens the cold water inlet 5, the hot water inlet 7, and the normal temperature inlet 6 while (determine) passing through the water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text