eline 402"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at block 1806, the method includes affecting the temperature of the transported fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the inhibit (affect)ing of heat transfer (block 1802) from the pipeline to the environment (e.g., when the external temperature is below a threshold) may maintain the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the promoting of heat transfer (block 1804) from the environment to the pipeline (e.g., when the external temperature is above a threshold) may increase the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid-transporting pipeline, and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to (affect) a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported, and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is necessary to make the block distance shorter than a specified length, e.g., said 10 km, or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one, for reducing the effect of (affect) the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100970425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the operation of the boiler 341 is stopped and the high temperature steam obtained by the operation of the heat pump 340 is blocked by blocking the inflow of water vapor through the boiler 341 to prevent (therefore) the backflow of the boiler 341"}, {"pat_id": "US-9370746-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a pressure pump that delivers supply water to the ro membrane module is operated at a constant operating pressure, a water volume of produced permeate water (pure water) becomes mailer than a required production volume of water, when a temperature of supply water is low or when a membrane is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100479757-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to (thus) low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, the controller 14 may receive (thus) the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor unit 11, and block the valve 13 when the temperature of the water in the water pipe rises above a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101373842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by measuring the temperature change of the hot water inside the hot water tank through the temperature sensor, if the temperature change of the hot water over time is greater than the reference value by stopping the operation of the heating unit, heating in the absence of hot water in the hot water tank the negative operation can be blocked to prevent (thus) defective or malfunction of the heating unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101583008-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, the bimetal 23 or 23 the heater power is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor, accordingly, the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats, and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200383900-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a cpu that controls a current controller to block a current flowing through the electrode plate when the temperature of the inflow water detected by the temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, in some embodiments, the control sub-system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 (process block 118)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, in such embodiments, fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40, for example, via (thus) one or more external fluid conduits 62, such as a hose (process block 98)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally or alternatively, determining the one or more fluid parameters associated with the fluid in the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 may include determining fluid temperature present within the tubing annulus 25, for example, via (thus) an upstream fluid temperature sensor 58a (process block 120)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "if, in block 7348, the differe