  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9023184-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, even in a case where the device has temperature variation that is caused when water is passed or stopped in the process of producing deionized water, a gap is not produced between the respective chambers and hence water leakage is not caused"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "wherein the monitoring (therefore) unit configured to monitor the state of the conduit unit by at least one of detecting a leakage occurrence at the conduit unit, determining a temperature at the conduit unit, determining a pressure at the conduit unit, determining a flow rate at the inside of the conduit unit or determining a ph-value of the fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, leakage monitoring is required, e.g., through distributed temperature monitoring to identify hot air escaping form the conduit unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102093874-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, the coupling by bearing is possible in a fermentation device operated at room temperature and normal pressure, but there is room for problems such as leakage and deformation due to thermal expansion in a drying device supplied with high-temperature and high-pressure dry air"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394, this is not significant enough to prevent (determine) the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change, or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100920963-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sealing material 60 is a protective layer for preventing the leakage preventing structure from being deteriorated due to expansion or contraction or deterioration of the structural material due to temperature change, and is preferably finished with an elastic material sealant in consideration of the behavior of the joint 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to (thus) contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101910492-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to (thus) contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by integrating on-site pressure sensing and temperature sensing, operating state monitoring (thus) on the heating pipelines and pipeline leakage analysis and early warning are realized without adding sensing devices"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at the moment of leakage, the temperature of the inner surface of the thermal insulation layer 6 is the temperature of the outer wall of the pipeline without leakage, that is ton=tol, and thus, the variation of the transient heat capacity of steam at the moment of leakage can be obtained by substituting tol into the formula (1) \u03b4q"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "and the variation of the temperature in the pipeline is less affected (thus) by an external environment, the process of solving the transient pressure by the leakage transient temperature is specifically as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "because (thus) collection analysis of the pressure sensors on the pressure waves are mature, and the variation of the transient temperature at the leakage point can be hardly embodied by data collected by the temperature sensors, a pipeline leakage early warning is realized by setting a pressure threshold value"}, {"pat_id": "US-12265759-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the daily construction process of heating pipelines, there will be problems such as pipeline leakage, but generally, the pipeline is tested manually on a regular basis to ensure the normal operation of the pipeline, or after receiving complaints from users, it may be because individual users can t receive (thus) the heating or the heating temperature is too low, so the pipeline detection will be carried out"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid-transporting pipeline, and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to (thus) a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported, and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the case of larger and longer pipeline, an amount of the liquid to be passed through a flow rate meter will be increased owing to an increase in volume change due to (thus) a change in the liquid temperature in the pipeline, and the sensitivity of the flow rate meter is lowered for a small amount of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is necessary to make the block distance shorter than a specified length, e.g., said 10 km, or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one, for reducing the effect of (thus) the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-9254221-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "because the role of the heating pipe, the temperature of the liquid in the pipeline will be elevated, and it has an advantage of comfortable and healthy to dispose the pipeline on the pad, it can prevent (thus) the leakage, and obtains higher safety"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a location of where the leakage is occurring may be determined by the controller when the temperature readings of these temperature sensors are compared while (determine) the water heater 10 is in the standby mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in another example, when determining a leakage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and third temperature sensors 114, 122 during evening hours (i.e., sleeping) when it is most likely the user will not require (determine) use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "although the leaked water may lose some heat during the wait period 695 while accumulating in the drain pipe 394, this is not significant enough to prevent (determine) the change in state of the temperature reading from the negative rate of change to the positive rate or change, or to prevent the increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 1, the control unit drives the temperature sensor at regular intervals, the heat pipe leakage monitoring (determine) device, characterized in that to cut off the power at the remaining time except the driving time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101025538-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the mounting table is provided with a plurality of temperature sensors 120 for monitoring (determine) whether leakage occurs in the heat pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receive (determine)r 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6) in the same manner as the temperature sensor 110a, it is possible to detect that leakage occurs when the humidity value becomes higher than the second detection signal of the neighboring sensing unit 100 because (determine) the humidity becomes higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if only the temperature sensor 110a is applied, if the temperature of the soil is lowered due to (determine) reasons other than leakage, in order to compensate for this, it is possible to compare the temperature and humidity sensing values together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture, if the inside gets wet due to (determine) snow or rain when exposed to the outside, the temperature sensor often malfunctions, and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (determine), the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art, so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure, especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}]</data>
