  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-2749860-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "are arranged on the base part (40) for sound measurement for the purpose of leak detection and/or for detecting the volumetric water usage via the hydrant (1) and/or for detecting water characteristic variables, such as pressure, ph-value, hardness, turbidity and temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data, system 10 component data, or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-12111007-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a conventional leak detection system is based on several models, which provide continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at some points along the pipeline with automated analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-6970808-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in choosing the optimum model, a leak detection system that provides continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at points along the pipeline, supported by automated analysis of the data is most ideal"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is a further aspect of the present invention to implement the aforementioned monitoring step by utilizing sensors which have been used in the oil industry, such as the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring, and/or the sensors used for leak detection, soil heating, and temperature mapping"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring that are disclosed in the first reference cited above, and/or the sensors used for leak detection, soil heating, and temperature mapping that are disclosed in the second set of references cited above"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by filling the sensing unit, it is possible to prevent the malfunction of the leak detection sensor due to (thus) the small amount of condensate formed in the water supply pipe due to the difference between the water supply temperature and the room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10036143-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent (thus) and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "for measuring or monitoring (thus) the temperature of the water flowing through the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent (thus) and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak