ative of normal use conditions or a leak using machine learning algorithms that can be trained over time with data fed into the system(s) such that the system can accurately identify (determine) whether sensor data is indicative of normal and/or abnormal conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a cross-sectional view showing a strainer installation state in another embodiment of the odor leak prevention apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100957464-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when rainwater or impurities pass through the movable plate mounted on the malodor prevention device, the movable plate is closed to prevent odor generated from the lower part of the sump well from leaking out through the grating"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is possible to prevent the water in the water storage tank 2 from leaking, and it is possible to surely switch between water storage and water discharge by opening and closing the drain hole 11c with the drain hole opening / closing lid 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to solve this problem, a number of techniques have been disclosed for preventing leakage of odor flowing back from the sewage pipe back to the rainwater pipe or rainwater collection tank, for example, to cover oil and access holes of the rainwater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "odor leak prevention deodorization system 100 of the rainwater collection tank of the present invention is installed in the rainwater collection tank (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone, but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-9828757-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "vacuum sewer systems operate inefficiently when water infiltration and inflow are present due to leaks and improper connections to storm water drains"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the machine-learning algorithm can be trained with data provided from the control unit server 104, data provided by the smart water valve 126, and data associated with the security system 148 to predict devices that are leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in response to providing the data from each of the devices in the monitored property 102 to the trained model, the trained model can produce a predicted device that is leaking based on the detection by the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "should the smart water valve produce a detection that water is leaking or the trained model predict a device that is leaking water in the monitored property 102, the control unit server 104 can provide that detection and/or prediction to the client device 122 of the property owner 120"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "similarly, the security system 148 can transmit a command to the smart water valve 126 to move the position of the ball valve 208 to open in response to the trained machine-learning model predicting no device is leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevent (predict)ed from leaking"}]</data>
</edge>
