  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water accumulate (increase)d in the rainwater infiltration basin penetrates from the bottom of the rainwater infiltration basin into the gap between the gravel or crushed stones in the foundation block, and is drained from a drain hole formed in the side circumference of the rainwater infiltration basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0016] the water retention block for a rainwater infiltration basin according to the invention is much lighter and easier to handle than a conventional water retention block, so that its volume can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715445-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the packing member interposed between the upper body and the rainwater collecting basin blocks the odor coming up from the sewer, thereby improving the living environment and preventing habitat for harmful insects such as flies and mosquitoes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100649520-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because the foreign matter is moved through the sewage canal 40, along with the sewage and sewage in several directions, so that the foreign matter is accumulated in the sewer 60 to block or narrow the sewer pipe so that the problem does not occur in the drainage of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional rainwater collecting facility provided on such a road surface has a problem that rainwater inflow to the soil is blocked because the collected rainwater is flowed as it is to the excellent canal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to (remove) the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101132847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 is a block diagram showing a state in which rain and earth inflow prevent (remove)ion device having a buoyancy chamber according to the first embodiment of the present invention is installed, fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to (remove) a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101545448-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[ the end of the horizontal channel section 133 is clogged by the partition wall 111c while (remove) the guide channel 132b formed by the horizontal channel section 133 is formed by the opening 135 formed in the partition wall 111c so that the initial rain can be discharged through the opening 135 to the interior of the discharge chamber 116, which will be described later, and the opening 135 is blocked to be openable by the opening / closing door 136"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39