  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in sewage or polluted small streams, contaminants are deposited on the bottom in sinking areas, lowlands, and bore areas, and when the flow rate increases during rainfall, the sewage power increases, causing the sediment to float and outflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100990483-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the screen 12 is installed in multiple stages on the sewage pipe 10 to prevent (cause) the inflow of contaminants into the stormwater chamber 11 by separating various contaminants in advance before the initial rainwater reaches the first opening and closing plate 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater is introduced into the inflow chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the debris receive (cause)r 123b during the process of passing through the inflow chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater from the inflow chamber 123a3 flows into the treatment chamber 123a4 and is processed by the treatment action of the contaminant filtration / adsorption means 123c while (cause) passing through the treatment chamber 123a4 and then into the outflow chamber 123a5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminants settle (cause)d in the excellent water collecting chamber 11 lower the degree of purification of excellent purification, the water is guided to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 so as not to feed water to the purified water supply water chamber 14, which is conducted through the drain portion 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive (cause) sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive (cause) sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, the screw screen 10 excludes coarse contaminants included in the initial rainwater during rainy weather and sediment contaminants deposited in the combined sewer pipe 2, and removes the coarse contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101024670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to (remove) the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the combined sewage pipe are simultaneously leaked, resulting in a high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067633-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to (remove) the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101095323-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is called cso (combined sewer overflow), and due to (remove) the initial rainfall, the pollutants on the surface and the contaminants settled in the consolidation sewers flow out at the same time, resulting in a very high concentration and load of the pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to (remove) the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133277-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the height of the purification device 1 of the present invention is lower than the height of the inclined drain conduit 2, so that the contaminants are smoothly conveyed to the contaminant collecting part 40, and also due to (remove) the heavy rain, the flow rate of rainwater may be high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer formed on the upper and lower trench conduits to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remaining rainwater is decayed to prevent the occurrence of odors or pests, and periodically operates the air diffuser to remove contaminants attached to the filtration device or the swash plate device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the discharge line 322 directs the pollutants and sludge inhaled through the backwater drainage pump 320 directly to the sewage treatment plant or designated wastewater treatment facility to prevent the effluent from being contaminated by the contaminants and sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the bottom of the cylindrical screen, the bottom is formed with a drain hole is formed by the coarse sediment freely dropped through the contaminant discharge pipe and the vortex discharged to the sewage pipe intermediate intermediate sediment removed from the cylindrical screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the initial rainwater accumulated at the tip of the screen body 11 together with the coarse contaminants and sediment contaminants may be discharged through the contaminant discharge pipe 17, which may cause a variety of problems such as a burden on the sewage pipe 4 or the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200368783-Y1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "inflow water is discharged through the discharge pipe 60, and the bulky contaminants are caught by the strainer 62 to prevent (remove) the inflow into the discharge pipe 60, thereby preventing the blockage of the discharge pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, with the coarse contaminants and sediment contaminants, the initial rainwater accumulated at the tip of the screen body 11 may be discharged through the contaminant discharge pipe 17 to cause various problems such as 