cation (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the contaminant discharge pipe 17 is not affected (remove) by the drain opening 22 of the vortex 21 by the double opening / closing valve 24, and always removes the coarse contaminant as the sewage pipe 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the intermediate contaminants included in the initial excellent water are temporarily blocked by the double opening / closing valve 24 sealing the drain hole 22 formed at the bottom of the vortex 21, and finally removed from the sewage pipe 4 when opened"}, {"pat_id": "US-12202741-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (remove), the particulates and other contaminants that can be dislodged and removed by backwashing the resin are caused to flow out the top of the tank, through the valve and are discharged to a suitable waste drain through the drain port c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to (remove) rain or the like, the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases, so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by automatically controlling the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in several stages according to the water level of the water channel 10, water flows in the water channel 10 so that the contaminants 40 can be quickly removed when the water level suddenly blows in rainy weather"}]</data>
