  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event of a short-term backwater in the dirty water channel and thus the connection line being closed, the water from the tap can be temporarily stored in dry weather and then drained off"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "according to one form of the invention, it is provided that the incorrect discharges are transferred into the latter due to (thus) a flow gradient between the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this takes advantage of the fact that in a separation system the dirty water channel is always lower than the rain water channel and thus the dirty or waste water in the rain water channel can get into the dirty water channel due to (thus) the natural flow gradient"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if the rainwater channel to the dirty water channel is not closed off, water can thus pass from the rainwater channel to the dirty water channel, but not vice versa"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event of a short-term backwater in the dirty water channel and thus the connection line being closed, the water from the tap can be temporarily stored in dry weather and then drained off"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "because of (thus) the rain water still flowing in small quantities through the rain water channel 2, the dirty water channel 4 experiences a second flush with rain water through the connecting line 5"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to (thus) the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}]</data>
