  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water accumulate (increase)d in the rainwater infiltration basin penetrates from the bottom of the rainwater infiltration basin into the gap between the gravel or crushed stones in the foundation block, and is drained from a drain hole formed in the side circumference of the rainwater infiltration basin"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0016] the water retention block for a rainwater infiltration basin according to the invention is much lighter and easier to handle than a conventional water retention block, so that its volume can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715445-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the packing member interposed between the upper body and the rainwater collecting basin blocks the odor coming up from the sewer, thereby improving the living environment and preventing habitat for harmful insects such as flies and mosquitoes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional rainwater collecting facility provided on such a road surface has a problem that rainwater inflow to the soil is blocked because the collected rainwater is flowed as it is to the excellent canal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to (remove) a malfunction of the first water