vided with the drainage device described in claim 13 , in addition to the effect of (therefore) claim 11 or 12 , rainwater and the like that have entered the first water conduit can be along the lower surface that is the inclined surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101008372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the blocking plate 120 is rotated upward by a hinge (not shown) by the water pressure of the mixed water which is mixed with the sewage and rainwater to the sewage pipe 11 while (therefore) opening the discharge conduit 110 and opened at the same time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a bad smell blocking member that prevent (therefore)s the coming offensive odor from dissipating to the outside of the grating, and discharges the rainwater that flows back to the outside of the grating when the rainwater rises in the conduit and the rainwater flows back from the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing from the outside of the grating 10 flows along the inclined upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122 and accumulates on the inclined lower upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122, and each of the malodors when the rainwater accumulated on the inclined lower upper surface of the blocking blade 122 is accumulated by a predetermined amount or more, the respective odor blocking blades are formed such that the lower portion of each odor blocking blade 122 faces the conduit due to (therefore) the weight of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the rainwater rises in the conduit due to (therefore) excessive rain, etc., and the rainwater flows back from the conduit, the rainwater flowing back from the conduit pushes up the inclined upper bottom surface of each odor blocking blade 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the