  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to (remove) a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39 to prevent (remove) the discharge of the rainwater to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at the end of the sewer pipe (1), the sewage discharge port (2) is normally closed to guide the sewage to the sewage treatment plant through the rainwater discharge chamber (3) to block the discharge of odors and to increase the amount of sewage into rainwater that flows during rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seals the rainwater receiving chamber (420) with the buoyancy of the rainwater (c), thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in treating