R-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive (therefore) sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upper inlet 111 may receive (therefore) sewage from which contaminants have been removed by the contaminant screen 103 and introduce it into the rainwater chamber 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater having contaminants from the open end 21 of the water inlet pipe 13, the first accommodation chamber 11a and the rainwater eddy pipe 20 and the sewage pipe p flowing into the length is vortex vortices along the circumference of the second accommodation chamber (11b) through the holes 22 of the excellent eddy pipe 20, thereby causing a eddy phenomenon"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for this reason, even when a large rainwater exceeding a design value flows into the rainwater treatment system according to the present invention, the pollutant having a large concentration of the contamination separated from the initial rainwater may be transferred to the second accommodation chamber 11b through the porous pipe 31 and the protrusion 50"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6164161-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "furthermore, it is possible to prevent rainwater (including condensation), dust, and the like from accumulating inside the welded portion between the water storage tank 10 and the valve chamber (30, 52) and causing corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 ha