  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to block the supply of river water or seawater backflowing to the stormwater chamber 110 to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-9580899-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, such end wall panels 82 act as a boundary block around the perimeter of the storm pod structure 10 and function to aid corresponding liquid retention chambers 76 in retaining the liquid or overflow water stored therein"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevent (therefore)ed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100795399-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the stormwater manager regularly checks the slope screen bar (4) and sand sedimentation chamber (5) of the stormwater chamber and periodically removes contaminants and sand by manpower"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receive (therefore)r 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm flows into the inlet chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the obstacle receive (therefore)r 123b during the passage through the inlet chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pollutant screening net 20 removes contaminants contained in the storm water flowing into the excellent stormwater chamber 11 from the outside and guides the contaminants to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 through the stormwater collecting chamber 11, a space is formed between the water collecting chamber 11 and the upper portion of the pollutant discharge chamber 12 and between the second partition 12a and the pollutant discharge chamber 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361427-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, since the holes 22 of the storm duct 20 are formed to be below the normal water level of the second accommodation chamber 11b, relocation of the contaminants suspended through the holes 22 and their backflow is prevent (therefore)ed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "US-8297880-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, because of their different use, storm chambers lack a multiplicity of small perforations in the sidewall, which necessarily characterize leaching chambers and weaken a sidewall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm flows into the inlet chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the obstacle receiver 123b during the passage through the inlet chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}]</data>
</edge>
