ion prevention device is flooded by flooding or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101254083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the valve spool 42 is always buoyant in the submerged state, the close contact surface 42a of the valve spool 42 remains in close contact with the seat surface 41b of the valve cylinder 41, and thus the air passage 41a of the valve cylinder 41 is blocked, and the surface water due to the flooding is blocked from flowing into the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "without proper maintenance, backwater valves can become blocked or stuck, giving building managers and homeowners a false sense of security that they will be protected during a flooding event"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however many homeowners and residents are not aware of the presence or operation of a backwater valve, and if the valve is closed due to a flooding event or blockage many residents will not be aware of it until sanitary sewage begins flowing back into their building"}]</data>
