, and also due to (remove) the heavy rain, the flow rate of rainwater may be high"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer formed on the upper and lower trench conduits to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the inner wall of the upper, lower trench conduits (50, 60) to form a water purification filtration layer 70 to prevent contamination of the rainwater is stored"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the structure further comprises a catchment supported to receive (carry) rainwater running from the roofing and at least one water-carrying conduit extending from the catchment to the enclosure interior so as to deposit rainwater running from the roof into the enclosure beneath the flooring"}, {"pat_id": "US-5239794-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at least one water carrying conduit 62 is provided extending from the catchment 60 to the interior of the enclosure formed by foundation 20 and floor 30, in particular the enclosure 25a, so as to deposit rainwater running from the roofing into the enclosure beneath the flooring 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101305591-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the wide diameter, it is easy for sediment to settle in conduits, and there is a high possibility that sewage from rainwater tosoil may leak into the body of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear (11, 12, 13), if necessary, the front side of each overflow wear (11) (12) (13) as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173254-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by preventing the rainwater from flowing into the sewer conduit 20 by the rotation of the wear 40, it is possible to maintain a constant treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant by adjusting the inflow amount into the sewage treatment plant, thereby maintaining excellent sewage treatment quality"}]</data>
