  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, in such embodiments, fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40, for example, via (thus) one or more external fluid conduits 62, such as a hose (process block 98)"}, {"pat_id": "US-4808290-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if pool water stops flowing through metal conduit 46 while (thus) electrical power continues to be supplied to field wiring block 366, then after approximately five minutes, the temperature of metal bar 384 and thermostatic switch 386 rises above the aforementioned predetermined temperature, and themostatic switch 386 opens"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "via the ion source block, the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set-point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358103-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the flexible conduit tube is wavy, so it is very easy to draw wires and is not subject to temperature changes, so there is no need for relaxation measures, and it is easy to prevent acid and corrosion resistance and has almost no condensation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the heater 610 of the heater unit 600 is disposed in the conduit 510 as in one embodiment of the present invention, the heater 610 is directly in contact with the fire water in the conduit 510, and the heater 610 can directly heat the fire water in the conduit 510, the heating efficiency and energy utilization efficiency of the fire water in the conduit 510 is excellent, thereby freezing the fire water in the conduit 510 quickly it can be heated to the above temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to (thereby) freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 702 and the secondary temperature sensor package 706 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent (thereby) the fluid within the fluid conduit system 720 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, a temperature or temperature range may be chosen at which the microprocessor 712 will add heat energy to the fluid in the fluid conduit system 720 before the water reaches 32 degrees fahrenheit to prevent (thereby) it from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 806 and the secondary temperature sensor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent (thereby) the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the system 1100 is configured for use on a fluid conduit system 1102 located within a structure 1101 to prevent (thereby) the fluid conduit system 1102 from damage due to freezing fluid upon detection of freezing conditions, such as the temperature of the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 and the temperature of the environment surrounding the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by placing the primary heating element 1120 and secondary heating element 1122 at the areas of the fluid conduit system 1102 with the coldest temperatures, the heating element may be turned on to prevent (thereby) the fluid within the conduit from freezing or defrost already frozen fluid within the fluid conduit"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1140 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may also turn on the heating elements to heat up the pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent (thereby) the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, a temperature or temperature range may be chosen for the fluid temperature and the environment temperature at which the control system 1140 will add heat energy to the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 before the water reaches 32 degrees fahrenheit to prevent (thereby) it from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent (thereby) fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1140 may turn on the heating elements 1120 and 1122 to prevent (thereby) fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value, the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time, and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1230 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may also turn on the heating element to heat up the fluid and pipes when the external environment temperature or the local environment temperature reaches a predetermined value to prevent (thereby) the fluid within the conduit from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent (thereby) fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature of the fluid reaches a certain value and if the environment temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control system 1230 may turn on the heated recirculation circuit 1220 to prevent (thereby) fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102 from freezing when the temperature reaches a certain value, the temperature is at or below a certain value for a predetermined period of time, and the temperature is at or below a certain value and the wind speed is at a certain value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tps2 and max time at second threshold temperature tpsmax provides a factor of safety to prevent (thereby) possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tss2 and max time at second threshold temperature tssmax provides a factor of safety to prevent (thereby) possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle12 and max time at second threshold temperature tle1max provides a factor of safety to prevent (thereby) possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tle22 and max time at second threshold temperature tle2max provides a factor of safety to prevent (thereby) possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second threshold temperature tet2 and max time at second threshold temperature tetmax provides a factor of safety to prevent (thereby) possible freezing of fluid due to unexpected wind, dips in temperature, or other unaccounted factors that may affect the temperature of the fluid within the fluid conduit system 1102"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, each of those devices are actuated in response to ambient air temperature and thus will serve to trickle water when the air temperature is near the freezing temperature of water, even though the temperature of the water in the conduit may be at a higher temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the actuation of the unit depends upon the water temperature within the conduit, the unit will only operate to trickle water when there exists a real danger that freezing may occur, thus minimizing water waste"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to anti-freezing devices, and in particular to temperature-activated assemblies that prevent (thereby) freezing and rupture of outdoor water-supply conduits"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "wherein the monitoring (therefore) unit configured to monitor the state of the conduit unit by at least one of detecting a leakage occurrence at the conduit unit, determining a temperature at the conduit unit, determining a pressure at the conduit unit, determining a flow rate at the inside of the conduit unit or determining a ph-value of the fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-12510435-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, leakage monitoring is required, e.g., through distributed temperature monitoring to identify hot air escaping form the conduit unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after subcritical wet oxidation treatment, the oxidation mixture exits the reactor vessel 20 via a conduit 22 and is heated by a heater 24 to supercritical water temperatures, in excess of 374 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additional oxidant, such as oxygen gas, air or chemical oxidant such as hydrogen peroxide or ozone, may optionally be added, via a conduit 26, to the oxidation mixture prior to the mixture entering the heater 24, or after heating the oxidation mixture to supercritical water temperatures via a conduit 26"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vapor phase in the subcritical wet oxidation reactor vessel 20 exits via a conduit 22 and enters a heater 24 which heats the vapor phase to supercritical temperatures, greater than 374 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the supercritical phase then flows via a conduit 30 and enters the heat exchanger 12 where it cools to subcritical temperatures, by heat exchange against the oxidation mixture entering the system, to give a mixture of condensed liquid and gases"}, {"pat_id": "US-5888389-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and (e) a supercritical water oxidation reactor connected to receive a partially reacted mixture from the heater through a second reaction conduit, the partially reacted mixture comprising partially oxidized feed mixture, the supercritical water oxidation reactor for maintaining the partially reacted mixture at a supercritical temperature and supercritical pressure for a time sufficient to oxidize substantially all organic material within the partially reacted mixture and produce a supercritical effluent"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to anti-freezing devices, and in particular to temperature-activated assemblies that prevent freezing and rupture of outdoor water-supply conduits"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1218293-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the purpose of the intercooler 118 is to cool the treated water to a temperature sufficiently low so as not to cause hardness in the untreated water passing through the heat exchanger to precipitate and form scale in the heat exchange cartridge 116 and the conduits feeding the untreated water from the heat exchange cartridge 116 to the water treatment cartridge 114"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1228003-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the purpose of the intercooler 118 is to cool the treated water to a temperature sufficiently low so as not to cause hardness in the untreated water passing through the heat exchanger to precipitate and form scale in the heat exchange cartridge 116 and the conduits feeding the untreated water from the heat exchange cartridge 116 to the water treatment cartridge 114"}]</data>
