ere blockage of the drainage from the building causes pressure buildup between the municipal sewer and the building, putting the building at risk of a backwater flood"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100498266-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it has the effect of (cause) preventing the blockage of flood gates, the blocking of running water, and the failure of drainage facilities such as pump stations"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this causes a flood condition, where blockage of the drainage from the building causes pressure buildup between the municipal sewer and the building, putting the building at risk of a backwater flood"}, {"pat_id": "US-11060313-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "should flood waters exceed the dfe 3, water will enter the building 1 through the drain holes 19 preventing the collapse of exterior wall 5a and damage to the building foundation 4 from buoyancy effects"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, through the drainage module and the flood control module, it is possible to quickly and actively respond to flooding in the event of a water leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the installation height of the flood detection sensor 210 is installed at a certain height from the bottom of the drain 101, not the bottom of the drain 101, so that it can be determined that flooding has occurred due to water leakage, not living water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by allowing only the drain hole 111 to pass through, and to improve the drainage effect by opening both the drain hole 111 and the through holes 112 and 112a when a water leak occurs, it is possible to prevent the spread of flood damage due to water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the installation height of the flood detection sensor 210 is installed at a certain height from the bottom of the drain 101, not the bottom of the drain 101, so that it can be determined that flooding has occurred due to water leakage, not living water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102306868-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by allowing only the drain hole 111 to pass through, and to improve the drainage effect by opening both the drain hole 111 and the through holes 112 and 112a when a water leak occurs, it is possible to prevent the spread of flood damage due to water leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-5004014-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in these structures, if a water pipe ruptures and the rupture goes undetected, as can occur when one is asleep or during a holiday or weekend, not only will the floor where the rupture occurred flood but the water will also drain to lower floors"}]</data>
