  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100930723-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the manhole structure in the present invention discharges the inflow water into the ground or drainage layers while (thus) collecting and storing the inflow water through the porous block of the infiltration tank, and rainfall or a lot of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by providing the guide block 66 on the upper side of the drainage passage 52, rainwater that suddenly overflows due to (thus) heavy rainfall or the like is prevented, so that flooding of the earths due to heavy rainfall can be stably prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "even in this case, the rainwater drainage port 62 is blocked by contaminants and is not drained, and thus the rainwater guide unit 50 cannot return to the first position p1, and thus the rainwater containing the contaminants may not be excluded at the next rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances, rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578551-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a bypass pipe for bypassing and discharging rainfall runoff exceeding the storage capacity of the storage unit, wherein the drain can be connected to the bypass pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the rainwater flowing in the valleys and the drainage channels is suddenly blown up by heavy rainfall, and the flow velocity is a real danger of erosion or collapse of the soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102335129-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, the conventional slope structure simply performs a drainage function to prevent collapse, and even if the inflow of polluted river water or polluted water due to rainfall flows into the interior of the slope structure, it cannot be purified and discharged, and there is a problem that may cause soil contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed for the building drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and some of the contaminants are considered in consideration of the low content of contaminants for the subsequent building drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to (therefore) the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a large amount of pollutants, and considers that the content of the pollutants in the subsequent road drainage is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and considers that the content of the contaminants is low in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102335129-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, the conventional slope structure simply performs a drainage function to prevent collapse, and even if the inflow of polluted river water or polluted water due to rainfall flows into the interior of the slope structure, it cannot be purified and discharged, and there is a problem that may cause soil contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446316-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sewage should be supplied with household sewage from homes or commercial buildings near sewer pipes, and rainwater quickly drains rainwater generated during rainfall or snowfall to prevent road flooding and to prevent contamination from rainwater splashing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in this way, the pollutants deposited on the road are transported to the road drainage due to (increase) rainfall, flowed into the sewer, and then discharged to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the present invention has been proposed to solve the above problems, and has been deposited on the road surface while (increase) having the road drainage capacity of the rain can smoothly drain the increased road surface drainage during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, the pollutants deposited on the road surface are sequentially transported by road drainage due to (increase) rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to (increase) the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, the pollutants deposited on the road are transported to the road drainage due to (increase) rainfall, flowed into the sewers, and then discharged to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the above structure can increase the treatment efficiency of high concentration pollutants drained through the road during the initial rainfall stage, but if it exceeds the treatment capacity of the maintenance tank due to (increase) the sudden rainfall, various pollutants deposited on the road are maintained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "including pollutants deposited on road surface during initial rainfall, even if the amount of drainage flows into the inlet of rainwater drainage is large can be stored to prevent (increase) the drainage of water back to the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the removal process of the pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of the pollutants in the road drainage due to (increase) the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage is applied to the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, the pollutants deposited on the road are transported to the road drainage due to (increase) rainfall, flowed into the sewer, and then discharged to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the pollutants deposited on the road surface are sequentially transported by road drainage due to (increase) rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to (increase) the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the road surface drainage treatment apparatus having an initial excellent filtration function according to the present invention has a road drainage capacity capable of smoothly draining the road drainage increased during rainfall, and is deposited on the road surface"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2598696-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "for example, in the event of a heavy rainfall, where road water or water from the pavement may leak into the one or more open-topped utility channels 20, the level of water can be eased by transferring the water from the one or more open-topped utility channels 20 to the storm water drain 360 via the utility channel drainage pipe 380"}]</data>
