  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101238571-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the cleaning operation, by installing the upstream order wall 10 to block the inflow of river water and drain the water of the cleaning section, the water is exposed in the low area of the puddle while the riverbed is exposed"}, {"pat_id": "US-10322951-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the water with removed contaminant is drained from the drain pipe 54 disposed on the upstream side of the electrostatic filter 53 to the outside system"}, {"pat_id": "US-5662801-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it may further have the capability of monitoring the flow of the feed stream throughout the system via (remove) the flow meter, controlling the main pump and prompting the operator to drain organic contaminants from the separating unit"}, {"pat_id": "US-5871648-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the vessel drain opens to remove all contaminant via (remove) the sludge discharge stream 50"}, {"pat_id": "US-5965027-A", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the vessel drain opens to remove all contaminant via (remove) the sludge discharge stream 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100763800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "actions increase water contamination, but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir, i.e., the bottom of the drainage sluice"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101042852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "actions increase water contamination, but confine water using a bottom drainage reservoir configured to discharge a large amount of water from the upstream of the stream through the bottom of the reservoir, i.e., the bottom of the drainage sluice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8961793-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, storm drains often are designed to not enter conventional wastewater treatment plants and directly enter open streams or the oceans, resulting in widespread outbreaks of disease, heavy metals contamination, and suspended solids, which adversely affect wildlife and human beings"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the difference in the detected rates of temperature change during the wait period 695 is explained by the position of the first temperature sensor 414 being located downstream of the condensate management portion 400 (i.e., the drain pipe 394) such that the leaking water is inhibited from entering the drain line 398 to be detected by the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "US-9611160-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first diluted steam could be a rinsing stream and could be combined with the treated stream either prior to their combined discharge to a drain, or prior to the carbonator (if present) and/or any further treatment section present or of the concentrated stream after the anodic oxidation"}]</data>
