  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102476350-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-0761560 (2007.09.18)accordingly, the present invention has been proposed to solve the above conventional problems, and an object of the present invention is to be installed in a drain manhole where a grating is installed to block odors rising from the drain manhole at normal times and to drain water in the event of sudden heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476350-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is installed in the sewer manhole where the grating is installed by these main components to block the odor rising from the sewer manhole in the odor blocking mode normally, and quickly switch to the drainage mode for smooth drainage in the event of sudden heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476351-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-0761560 (2007.09.18)accordingly, the present invention has been proposed to solve the above conventional problems, and an object of the present invention is to be installed in a drain manhole where a grating is installed to block odors rising from the drain manhole at normal times and to drain water in the event of sudden heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476351-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is installed in the sewer manhole where the grating is installed by these main components to block the odor rising from the sewer manhole in the odor blocking mode normally, and quickly switch to the drainage mode for smooth drainage in the event of sudden heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312015-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if a backflow phenomenon of sewage occurs inside the catchment manhole in a low zone due to guerrilla heavy rain, the upper structure of the catchment manhole is configured to be lifted up to block the inlet of the barrier fastening frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200351993-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, when the water level of the sewage collected in the manhole is increased due to excessive sewage or heavy rain in the manhole, the level of the sewage is increased and the cover blocking the discharge hole rises due to the sewage level so that the slope is forcibly opened"}, {"pat_id": "US-11008747-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, as with conventional separate sewer manholes, it should be understood that in exceptional use, such as during heavy rain, flooding and/or blockage, the first chamber may be in liquid communication with the second chamber via the first access port and/or the second access port"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100758730-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and when the heavy rain is to be introduced into the interior through the through groove 310 formed in the manhole cover 200, at this time, the disk packing 350 fixed to the rotating shaft 331 is a manhole cover formed with the through groove 310 by being in close contact with the bottom of the (200) it is possible to prevent the leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100758730-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the ring packing is interposed between the manhole frame and the manhole cover and the disk packing is in close contact with the lower portion of the through groove can further obtain the effect of preventing the leakage through the through groove during the heavy rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100758730-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the ring packing is interposed between the manhole frame and the manhole cover and the disk packing is in close contact with the lower portion of the through groove can further obtain the effect of preventing the leakage through the through groove during the heavy rain"}]</data>
