  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify (determine) a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify (determine) a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1) determining whether the leak is on the a cold side or a hot side 2) identifying (determine) a first test manifold 112 and identifying a first fixture 122 associated with that first test manifold 112 3) changing the temperature of the pipelines 114 of the first test manifold 112 (i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the user 102 can temperature test the pipelines 114 of all of the manifolds 112 for the half bath vanity sink 842, the half bath toilet 840, hose bib 1 810, and hose bib 2 812 to see if the leak 154 is before or after each manifold 112 of each fixture 112 and to identify (determine) point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}]</data>
