  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-12492132-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "blockages to prevent (thus) blockages, a mesh with smaller openings than the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle must be in place upstream of the the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if access to the sewer line is provided upstream of the obstruction, use of a nozzle such as nozzle 18 to clear a small opening through the blockage, and allow the flow through the obstruction and on down the sewer, enables use of the nozzle 20 without concern that the area between the nozzle and the obstruction will become (thus) flooded"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, plugs may be positioned both upstream of the nozzle and downstream of the obstruction for blocking flow from upstream in the sewer line and creating a flow restriction downstream of the obstruction"}, {"pat_id": "US-12492132-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "blockages to prevent (thus) blockages, a mesh with smaller openings than the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle must be in place upstream of the the open area of a static nozzle or the smallest opening in an adjustable nozzle"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if access to the sewer line is provided upstream of the obstruction, use of a nozzle such as nozzle 18 to clear a small opening through the blockage, and allow the flow through the obstruction and on down the sewer, enables use of the nozzle 20 without concern that the area between the nozzle and the obstruction will become (thus) flooded"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the cavitation nozzle 10 is used to cause cavitation in a water waste stream passing therethrough to aid in the remediation and purification of the waste stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-6733727-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "although most systems utilize transducers to create cavitation, some systems utilize the pressure drop across a nozzle to induce (cause) cavitation downstream of the nozzle throat"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, plugs may be positioned both upstream of the nozzle and downstream of the obstruction for blocking flow from upstream in the sewer line and creating a flow restriction downstream of the obstruction"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-8703065-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the nozzle may be configured to produce at least one fine stream that allows at least some of the water to evaporate while in the air, which leaves the salt to fall into the collection pit 162"}, {"pat_id": "US-9005310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the nozzle may be configured to produce at least one fine stream that allows at least some of the water to evaporate while in the air, which leaves the salt to fall into the collection pit 162"}, {"pat_id": "US-8312930-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fluid stream exiting from discharge nozzle 36 is at such a high pressure that the stream can extend through the perforations to break up pluggage also found incrusting the gravel pack"}, {"pat_id": "US-10926284-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the collector(s) may be configured to receive a volume of water projected at least the horizontal distance from the nozzles, e.g., the water jet/stream from the nozzle should generally traverse at least the distance of displacement between the nozzle and the collector, to the extent it is aimed to reduce water loss"}]</data>
</edge>
