  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-S5924319-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in view of the above, the present inventor has based on the assumption that it is effective to use a correlation method in order to eliminate the influence of irregular fluctuations in pressure gradient when estimating the location of a leak in a pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pipeline in which pressure gradient detectors are attached to the upstream and downstream sides, and a device for detecting the occurrence (influence) of leakage in the pipeline is connected to these detectors, the device comprising"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in practice, the pressure gradient , fluctuations occur irregularly due to (influence) turbulence in the liquid flowing in the pipeline, noise in the measurement system, etc., and if the leakage is minute, changes in the pressure gradient caused by the leakage are buried in the irregular fluctuations, it is not possible to detect changes in the pressure gradient simply by taking an average"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a pipeline in which pressure gradient detectors are attached to the upstream and downstream sides, and a device for detecting the occurrence (therefore) of leakage in the pipeline is connected to these detectors, the device comprising"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5924320-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in practice, the pressure gradient , fluctuations occur irregularly due to (therefore) turbulence in the liquid flowing in the pipeline, noise in the measurement system, etc., and if the leakage is minute, changes in the pressure gradient caused by the leakage are buried in the irregular fluctuations, it is not possible to detect changes in the pressure gradient simply by taking an average"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the case of pipeline leakage, no phenomena of obvious free outflow and flow reduction of steam occur because of the presence of the thermal insulation layer (6), and therefore pressure gradients upstream and downstream of the leakage point are approximately the same, and after being stabilized, the pressures restore an original pressure distribution along the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_63", "text": "when an on-off event happens to the heating supply pump unit at the starting end of the pipeline, a great gradient variation of the pressure in the pipeline may be caused, which can cause a false leakage early warning easily"}]</data>
</edge>
