  <data key="d5">["loss", "pipe", "cracking", "corrosion", "earth", "pvc", "connection", "service", "repair", "project", "void", "sagging", "sewer", "weather", "action", "variation", "joint", "aging", "body", "activity", "portion", "wastewater", "material", "bending", "pressure", "life", "anomaly", "use", "dislocation", "foundation", "construction", "crack", "separation", "leakage", "year", "structure", "cause", "breakage", "ground", "bed", "ageing", "conduit", "engineering", "degradation", "pipeline", "load", "subsidence", "safety", "soil", "defect", "fluctuation"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["have", "result", "threaten", "suffer", "lead", "appear", "crack", "step", "include", "occur", "increase", "support", "cause", "age", "be", "break", "flow out", "coexist", "lift", "bury"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100730651-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines cause cracks, breakage, or stepped joints due to aging of the pipeline itself, subsidence of the underground ground or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground, and the wastewater inside the pipeline flows out through the broken portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100810555-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines, such as concrete pipes, pvc pipes, and conduits, have defects such as cracking, breakage, or separation of connections due to ageing of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground ground, or variations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102063829-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines such as sewer pipes buried underground cause sagging and breakage due to aging of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground bed, or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "with the service life continuous to increase, the pipelines will gradually aging and out of repair, and thus suffer with the coexisted engineering defects of cracking, corrosion and subsidence"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the pipelines suffer with structural defects including cracking, corrosion, and subsidence, directly lifting the subsidence pipeline may cause the pipelines to break structure, which threatens the safety of the construction"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, various engineering defects can occur (thus) in the buried pipelines in service all year around, and they include the subsidence, corrosion and cracking"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "cracks are prone to appear in the subsidence due to (thus) local bending, and corrosion usually occurs throughout the body of most pipelines"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100810555-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines, such as concrete pipes, pvc pipes, and conduits, have defects such as cracking, breakage, or separation of connections due to (thus) ageing of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground ground, or variations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "with the service life continuous to increase, the pipelines will gradually aging and out of repair, and thus suffer with the coexisted engineering defects of cracking, corrosion and subsidence"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the pipelines suffer with structural defects including cracking, corrosion, and subsidence, directly lifting the subsidence pipeline may cause the pipelines to break structure, which threatens the safety of the construction"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, various engineering defects can occur (thus) in the buried pipelines in service all year around, and they include the subsidence, corrosion and cracking"}, {"pat_id": "US-6243483-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "soil subsidence, local construction projects, seismic activity, weather, and degradation caused by normal use can also lead to defects and anomalies in a pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "subsidence is mainly because that the dislocation of the pipe joints or loss of foundation supporting materials caused by the fluid leakage at the cracks of the pipelines can result in the void, thus the subsidence occurs under the action of the upper load"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the pipelines suffer with structural defects including cracking, corrosion, and subsidence, directly lifting the subsidence pipeline may cause the pipelines to break structure, which threatens the safety of the construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102063829-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines such as sewer pipes buried underground cause sagging and breakage due to aging of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground bed, or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "US-11473713-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "subsidence is mainly because that the dislocation of the pipe joints or loss of foundation supporting materials caused by the fluid leakage at the cracks of the pipelines can result in the void, thus the subsidence occurs under the action of the upper load"}]</data>
</edge>
