in the pipeline 510 to prevent (influence) freezing by freezing of the pipeline 510"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to (influence) freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described in detail above, in order to prevent (influence) the pipeline from which fire water is discharged from a fire hydrant, a hose reel, a fire truck, etc., freezing and freezing in the winter, the water temperature is detected in direct contact with the fire water in a pipeline such as a fire hydrant, a hose reel, or a fire truck"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "using the latent heat signatures associated with phase changes of a process fluid (in this case sulphur) to identify (influence) solidification or melting of the process fluid at locations along a pipeline is not dependent on a particular melting or freezing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline, and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of (influence) heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline, which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to prevent (influence) pipelines from freezing and bursting at temperatures below zero during the winter, using the configuration of the hot water supplying system 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to (cause) contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring (cause) data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data, system 10 component data, or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12111007-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a conventional leak detection system is based on several models, which provide continuous monitoring (cause) of pressures, temperatures, and flow at some points along the pipeline with automated analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the method may further include determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify (cause) a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify (cause) a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1) determining whether the leak is on the a cold side or a hot side 2) identifying (cause) a first test manifold 112 and identifying a first fixture 122 associated with that first test manifold 112 3) changing the temperature of the pipelines 114 of the first test manifold 112 (i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by performing time based temperature checks, the user 102 may determine that pipeline 114c has water flowing down towards the leak 154 at the main water entrance 108 to the property 104 and through pipeline 114c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the user 102 can temperature test the pipelines 114 of all of the manifolds 112 for the half bath vanity sink 842, the half bath toilet 840, hose bib 1 810, and hose bib 2 812 to see if the leak 154 is before or after each manifold 112 of each fixture 112 and to identify (cause) point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after performing this initial temperature test, the user 102 knows that pipeline 114c is a distribution line 118 and is most likely the pipeline 114 leading to the leak 154 because of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "11-18, because the hot water will be leaking out through the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 containing an underground leak 154 which will make the surrounding area around the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 and floors above the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably warmer via touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1612, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the user 102 may safely assume and determine that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1714, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1814, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 126 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-6970808-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in choosing the optimum model, a leak detection system that provides continuous monitoring (cause) of pressures, temperatures, and flow at points along the pipeline, supported by automated analysis of the data is most ideal"}, {"pat_id": "US-8502687-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the determination module 302 determines the pipeline 100 works normally upon the condition that the fluid temperatures falls out of an allowable range or the leaks occur to the pipeline 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data and the like"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data, system 10 component data, or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-12111007-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a conventional leak detection system is based on several models, which provide continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at some points along the pipeline with automated analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-6970808-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in choosing the optimum model, a leak detection system that provides continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at points along the pipeline, supported by automated analysis of the data is most ideal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to (thus) contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in