  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for reference, the rainwater discharge structure using a single pump (p) is difficult to achieve the normal rainwater discharge of the transfer pipe far from the pump due to the increase in the volume of the transfer pipe (p1) when the construction length of the storage block 10 is long"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage pump is provided with a water level sensor to drain the stagnant water while (therefore) the position of the sediment detector descends to the settled contaminant surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a contaminant that is provided on the bottom of the drain pump to prevent (therefore) the sediment settled in the non-point pollution reduction facility is not drained by the drain pump it characterized in that it comprises a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the sediment detecting device is formed of a non-flowing material to support the weight of the drain pump on the surface of the contaminant, and the contact area with the contaminant is formed to a predetermined width to prevent (therefore) the sediment detecting device is inserted into the contaminant it is done"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the discharge line 322 directs the pollutants and sludge inhaled through the backwater drainage pump 320 directly to the sewage treatment plant or designated wastewater treatment facility to prevent (therefore) the effluent from being contaminated by the contaminants and sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414264-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit operates the cleaning pump 23 installed in the reverse injection pipe 21 to pressurize the rainwater backflow and spray through the injection nozzle 19 at a high pressure to collect the contaminants and contaminants accumulate (therefore)d in the mesh filter 5"}, {"pat_id": "US-5662801-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it may further have the capability of monitoring the flow of the feed stream throughout the system via (therefore) the flow meter, controlling the main pump and prompting the operator to drain organic contaminants from the separating unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100895623-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101053877-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200339290-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "small water pump protection supporting box the present invention relates to a water pump protection support for protecting an agricultural water pump installed in an outdoor field, and more particularly, to an improved small water pump protection support for preventing corrosion in an exposed state such as rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200339290-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1) it can protect and support the water pump from the infrared, ultraviolet ray and rainy weather in outdoor field to prevent corrosion and extend the life of the water pump"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first rainwater retaining pipe 5 is parallel to the sewer pipe 1 up to the location corresponding to the underground water diversion chamber 2, the portion from the top of the drainage pit 14 at the lower end of the pit 13 for pumping water gradually descends downward from the sewer line 1 while tilting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the buoyancy material 20 is provided in a wet space in which the stagnant water is formed, it is preferable that the buoyant material 20 is provided on the drain pump 10 with a material that does not rust because it may contaminate the stagnant water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200295999-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purpose is to prevent the failure and wear of the submersible pump 60 due to frequent starting and stopping of the submersible pump 60 for use of rainwater in toilet water or landscape water, thereby prolonging its life"}]</data>
</edge>
