e 402 provides a volume for collecting water introduced into the concrete structure 400 due to leakage of water supply pipes or inflow of rainwater, and a worker is provided with a water pump (hereinafter, not shown) separately provided through the inspection opening 401"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first rainwater retaining pipe 5 is parallel to the sewer pipe 1 up to the location corresponding to the underground water diversion chamber 2, the portion from the top of the drainage pit 14 at the lower end of the pit 13 for pumping water gradually descends downward from the sewer line 1 while tilting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200324955-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the sewage is treated in the same way as above, and the rainwater that is exceeding the sewage treatment amount (exactly diluted sewage mixed with rainwater) is pumped by the rainwater transfer pump (bar), and the rainwater distribution tank (3) next, the supernatant is precipitated in the storm sedimentation basin (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200295999-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purpose is to prevent the failure and wear of the submersible pump 60 due to frequent starting and stopping of the submersible pump 60 for use of rainwater in toilet water or landscape water, thereby prolonging its life"}]</data>
