  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101006852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the soil aquifer treatment has no water flow in the reservoir, so if it is operated for a long time, contaminants accumulate on the bottom of the reservoir, causing the blockage to be dried periodically"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101006852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the soil aquifer treatment has no water flow in the reservoir, so if it is operated for a long time, contaminants accumulate on the bottom of the reservoir, causing the blockage to be dried periodically"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2486988-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is thus possible, by reducing the contamination of the groundwater entering the reservoir or in the groundwater (eg over several cleaning cycles), to clean the groundwater located in the corresponding aquifer and thus to transfer the layer into a substantially uncontaminated layer"}]</data>
</edge>
