  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11679993-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the occurrence of biofouling, which is expected in a typical treated wastewater stream and associated wastewater handling equipment, it is beneficial for the tss sensor 5a to include a wiper system (not shown per se) which periodically cleans the face of the sensor component (not shown per se) of the tss sensor 5a"}, {"pat_id": "US-8097212-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the simplest way to prevent biofouling of the platinum redox sensor is to locate it in a strongly flowing part of the water stream in the pipe, e.g., away from the walls"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3468925-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the method may further comprise directing overflow wastewater to the overflow wastewater stream responsive to the sensor measuring a concentration of contaminants exceeding (increase) the threshold concentration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the effluent stream, the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant, such as a biologically tolerant compound, a biologically inhibit (increase)ory compound, and / or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation, has reached a predetermined value or trend, value, or trend, so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream, downstream from, or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a contaminant sensor configured to measure a concentration of a contaminant in a wastewater stream receive (increase)d from the waste outlet"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "receive (increase) a measured concentration of the contaminant in the wastewater stream from the contaminant sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "claim_20", "text": "receive (increase) a measured concentration of the contaminant in the reduced ph wastewater stream from the contaminant sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the contaminant were lead (pb) in this example, the conductivity of the water would increase from about 200 \u03bcs/cm in the feed water stream to 2000 \u03bcs/cm in the waste water stream, which would significantly increase detection sensitivity and reduce measurement time of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminant sensor 175 is positioned in the waste water stream, the detection sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is effectively increased compared to positioning it the feed water stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the readings of the contaminant sensor 175 are affected (increase) by the water quality (which includes the water s chemistry and other factors) of the waste water stream, and the water quality should be understood to properly deduce the concentration of contaminants in the feed water stream based on the readings of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the processor 190 receive (increase)s input from the water quality sensor module 185 and the contaminant sensor 175 to calculate the contaminant concentration in the waste water stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, by positioning the contaminant detection system 170 in the waste water stream where ions of contaminants are preconcentrated by the water treatment module 110, the effective sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the effluent stream, the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant, such as a biologically tolerant compound, a biologically inhibitory compound, and / or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation, has reached a predetermined value or trend, value, or trend, so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream, downstream from, or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-8097212-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the simplest way to prevent biofouling of the platinum redox sensor is to locate it in a strongly flowing part of the water stream in the pipe, e.g., away from the walls"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the difference in the detected rates of temperature change during the wait period 695 is explained by the position of the first temperature sensor 414 being located downstream of the condensate management portion 400 (i.e., the drain pipe 394) such that the leaking water is inhibit (determine)ed from entering the drain line 398 to be detected by the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in many situations these changes in pressure upstream of the devices while (determine) there being no flow detected by the flow sensors would be indicative of a leak upstream of the buildings"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "9c, background noise is filtered from the sensor signal(s) to determine building movement, detect upstream leaks and possibly take remedial action in the depicted process 900-3"}, {"pat_id": "US-12264083-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the online multi-sensor module is especially configured to automatically analyze the water upstream of the treatment module, thereby obtaining one or more water parameters indicative of properties of organisms in the untreated water"}]</data>
