r is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor, accordingly, the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats, and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200325952-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heat transfer unit 150 checks the temperature of the washing water at all times and the washing water temperature monitoring (thus) sensor 152 to block the operation of the heater when the temperature of the washing water is above a predetermined predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200383900-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a cpu that controls a current controller to block a current flowing through the electrode plate when the temperature of the inflow water detected by the temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, in some embodiments, the control sub-system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 (process block 118)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, in such embodiments, fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40, for example, via 