  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the present embodiment, predetermined seismic load is selected in consideration of the material and the capacity of the water tank 5, and for example, when the vibration energy of water is added to the predetermined earthquake load by an earthquake load, it can be determined by the strength of an earthquake that may cause deformation, breakage, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "as described above, if the vibration due to (cause) the earthquake is absorbed, breakage or damage of the water tank can be prevented, and thus the life of the water tank can be extended"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100653866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a concrete tank has a problem in that the cracking occurs over time due to (thus) the characteristics of concrete even if the waterproofing is thoroughly performed during construction, and in particular, there is a problem of cracking in case of uneven settlement of the ground and an earthquake"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100653866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention thus achieved by forming a storage tank using a plurality of tubes, first, the construction is simple and quick, and there is no cracking caused by uneven settlement or earthquake"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the present embodiment, predetermined seismic load is selected in consideration of the material and the capacity of the water tank 5, and for example, when the vibration energy of water is added to the predetermined earthquake load by an earthquake load, it can be determined by the strength of an earthquake that may cause deformation, breakage, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5, a plurality of dampers 10 are formed on a side of the water tank 5 which is in contact with the ground, and a plurality of dampers 10 are installed when a seismic load exceeds a predetermined seismic load, and an earthquake load is transmitted to induce (cause) plastic deformation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "by installing a plurality of vertical and horizontal beams to prevent (cause) bending deformation between the lower part and the floor, it serves to stably and firmly support the side load transmitted from the water tank body 2 when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3906965-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, if the aquarium itself is aged, the tank wall made of concrete may crack due to earthquakes and leak water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101837911-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, in the case of an immovable settlement caused by an earthquake or the like, there is a problem that the connection between the panels is broken, and leakage occurs in the broken part, thereby losing the function as a water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "seismic edge reinforcement means for reinforcing the connection between the unit panels on one side and the other side provided in multiple stages on one side and the other side of the peripheral edge of the water tank body to prevent (thereby) leakage of water from the peripheral edge when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seismic edge reinforcement means for reinforcing the connection between the unit panels on one side and the other side provided in multiple stages on one side and the other side of the peripheral edge of the water tank body to prevent (thereby) leakage of water from the peripheral edge when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as shown in the drawing, the seismic smc water tank (hereinafter referred to as water tank ) according to the present invention is capable of prevent (thereby)ing water leakage from occurring in the water tank by improving seismic performance when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the present invention is a useful invention that can prevent water leakage from occurring when the lower portions of the unit panels 22 of the lowermost layer of the water tank body 2 flow outward when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "by reinforcing the connection between the two, it serves to prevent (thereby) leakage from occurring at the peripheral edge of the water tank body 2 when an earthquake occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102297498-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, by reinforcing the connection state of the circumferential edge of the water tank through the earthquake-resistant edge reinforcing means 5, a gap is generated in the circumferential edge of the water tank during the release of an earthquake to prevent (thereby) leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5, a plurality of dampers 10 are formed on a side of the water tank 5 which is in contact with the ground, and a plurality of dampers 10 are installed when a seismic load exceeds a predetermined seismic load, and an earthquake load is transmitted to induce plastic deformation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101832706-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "for this purpose, it is possible to prevent the structural damage of the waterproof tank top-down resilient dry pad 1 by allowing the base plate 10 to flow during the earthquake through the elongate hole 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102101310-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the present invention also has the effect of continuously circulating water as a circulation device is installed to prevent the water swelling inside the water tank when an earthquake occurs.1 is a cross-sectional view of an example of a drainage reservoir having an internal circulation device according to the present invention"}]</data>
