  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": ".1 is a block diagram of an initial excellent storage processing system using a storage tank according to the present invention, 2 is a block diagram of the hydraulic pressure prevent (produce)ing means extracted from fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345790-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the drain pipe (yt pipe) as described above is provided to maximize the anaerobic efficiency by blocking the oxygen transfer to the fourth anaerobic tank 4 while (produce) overflowing (overflow) by the hydraulic pressure difference"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "moving said block of ice upwardly in said tank by hydraulic pressure of incoming salt water and melting the upper portion of said block of ice by indirect heat exchange with the salt water feed prior to entry of said feed into (produce) said column and withdrawing pure water from the upper portion of the tank between the top of said tank and the top of said ice block"}, {"pat_id": "US-4164854-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the hydraulic pressure acting upon the lower surface area of the ice block produces an upward force which becomes highest at the junction of the tank wall"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sealing the tank against ground water increases the tendency for in-ground tanks to collapse under the increased hydraulic pressure differential between high ground water and the tank interior"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101047186-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "other factors to consider include water pressure, seawater, loads when large fish collide, the size and material of the tank, the waterproofing and finishing materials that take into account the hydraulic pressure, and the selection of materials to prevent fatal toxicity and corrosion to the fish"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100598365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because large water tanks, which are largely divided from large ones, are more likely to leak due to hydraulic pressure in the case of minor gaps and ground subsidence"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "during periods of high ground water levels, this leakage enabled additional fluid to flow into the tank to compensate for the increased hydraulic pressure of surrounding ground water and water saturated soil"}]</data>
