  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5295753-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "for this reason, the precipitation of salt in the connection pipe does not block the connection pipe and prevent the supply of the cleaning liquid from the cleaning agent tank to the cleaning liquid tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102052855-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to control the discharge level of the treated wastewater, and to selectively block the supply of microbubbles inside the separation tank to use the separation tank as a sedimentation tank, but to induce precipitation in the vertical direction or inclined direction downward to maximize the precipitation efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102422847-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, it is possible to prevent iron precipitation through real-time ph measurement, and it is possible to provide a waste liquid decomposition monitoring device that can be used for maintenance of the uv reaction tank by checking the ph when washing the lamp in the uv reaction tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the waste water passing through the bypass pipe 20 is treated water that does not pass only the filtration tank 17, and is discharged through precipitation in the apparatus, so that almost contaminants are removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle (remove) in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101580859-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "[ therefore, the gravity type precipitation in the pretreatment tank and the primary treatment water in which the sediment and the contaminants are removed by the trapping net 110 are flowed to the filtration treatment tank 20 through the primary treatment water inflow pipe 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101779726-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in which after-precipitation process of a batch reaction tank is combined with an inverse filter module for discharging only the filtrate filtered out in treated water while (remove) separating fine contaminant particles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive (remove) the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102268655-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a precipitation treatment unit 300 provided to receive (remove) the desorbed liquid separated from the screen dehydration unit 200 in a treatment tank 310 to separate sediment contaminants in a precipitation method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle (remove) in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to provide an aeration/precipitation tank assembly in the system for removing contaminants which sprays air laden water into an air column to further oxidize the contaminants contained in the water while (remove) maintaining the system water pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction, and sends it to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to precipitate and remove the solid material, and then to the primary treatment tank (13), and then to the primary precipitation tank (5a)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in the primary aeration tank (3a), when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions, they are sent to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the main feature of the conventional immersion-membrane separation method in the field of water quality, which is this field, is to circulate the water in the water tank up and down to prevent precipitation of suspended solids or decay of stored water, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the stirring device or the water stirrer 222 is formed so that a shaft having a plurality of blades is rotated by a driving motor so as to prevent precipitation of the nitrification solution introduced from the aerobic tank and thereby prevent decay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the aerobic tank is equipped with an aeration device or a stirring device to form aeration using air or agitation using an agitator to prevent decay due to precipitation of sludge in the anoxic tank and to supply external carbon sources such as methanol"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100631373-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the anaerobic tank and the anaerobic tank, sludge is deposited due to (therefore) the sediment in the introduced wastewater and the returned wastewater, that is, denitrification or precipitation of phosphorus-overtake microorganisms"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the electrolytic waste liquid and the precipitating accelerator are not mixed uniformly, and the undrawn salt from the supernatant of the precipitation tank can be removed from the electrodeposition / adsorption unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an electrolysis device installed in the aerobic iron precipitation tank, the electrolysis module having an electrode mounted thereon, and an insoluble precipitate precipitated by reaction of an oxide produced by electrolysis of the electrolysis module and phosphate contained in the mixed solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the organic material and phosphorus are removed by the oxygen-free tank 40, the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50, and the electrolysis device 60, and nitrogen is removed in the nitrification and denitrification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 removes organic substances by metabolic activity of microorganisms, oxidizes ammonia nitrogen and nitrite nitrogen to nitrate nitrogen by oxygen supplied through a blower, and causes electrolysis of iron or aluminum electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102568017-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "the electrolysis unit 50 receive (produce)s the water filled in the precipitation tank 40 and electrolyzes it"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315874-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1b, is a modification of the a 2 / o method to increase the removal efficiency of phosphorus and nitrogen, wastewater through the first settling tank 100 anaerobic reactor 200, the first anoxic reactor 300, the first aerobic oxidation tank 400, the second anoxic reactor 500, the second aerobic reactor 600 and the second precipitation tank 700, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100387324-B1", "para_