st collecting pipe 17 may be directly supplied to the storage tank 20 or may be supplied to the storage tank 20 via (cause) the planter block 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "9, rainwater supplied to the storage tank 20 through the water collection pipe 16 or the second water collection pipe 35 directly from the rainwater collection well 10 or via (cause) the planter block 30 is stored in the storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3a and 3b are enlarged cross-sectional views showing the side inlet and outlet of the drain tank having functions of automatic odor blocking and prevent (cause)ing the inflow of pests according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5a and 5b are cross-sectional views illustrating a buoyancy part of a drainage tank having a function of automatically blocking odors and prevent (cause)ing the inflow of pests according to a modified example of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102284595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 6, in the drain tank having the function of automatically blocking odors and prevent (cause)ing the inflow of pests of the present invention, the sewage water introduced through the upper inlet 12 opened at the top of the main body 10 first ( 1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in other words, when the torrential rain starts, an overflow phenomenon may occur due to (cause) insufficient space accommodated in the first storage tank 140, the second storage tank 220, and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, rainwater flowing into each water collection tank 41 of the road block 40 while (cause) moving along the road surface 100 does not directly flow into the filling pipe 52 disposed in the filling section 41a, but settles in the sedimentation section 41b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102671842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pipe 46 is arranged at a certain inclination when connecting the lower end of the drain hole 42c and the upper edge of the water tank 20, which prevent (cause)s rainwater accumulated in the pair of water receiving blocks 42a and 42b from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to (cause) the overload problem of the above-described wastewater storage tank (30), it is inevitable to install the above-described frame (61) and rainwater blocking tent (60), which requires a lot of effort and cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to (cause) this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater receive (cause)r 20, the treatment tank 40, and the first partition wall 50 combine block pieces divided into two upper and lower stages, respectively, to form a partitioned water tank, and the upper and lower two block pieces are formed of a connection pin or a metal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is well known that the rainwater receive (cause)r 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40 formed by the combination structure of such block pieces may be rectangular or circular, and the entire block may be formed in one tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "dropping is placed on the concrete foundation and connected to the bolt nut in the transverse direction and the end wall plate is attached to the column along the rainwater tank block requiring (cause) the wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208312-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the sediment is separated by stages through the fine holes of the primary filtration network and the bottom plate to provide a rainwater catchment for the road equipped with a filtration tank to prevent the drainage blockage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because (remove) the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early 