th each other and gradually become (thus) lower toward the prefabricated kit rainwater storage tank 170"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226524-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-0938223 is difficult to form a wide enough space for cleaning and maintenance after installation of rainwater storage tank because (thus) the stand block located inside the rainwater storage tank is rectangular or square hexahedron shape, side block, when assembling the stand block, the upper block and the lower block, it is difficult to correct construction errors and it is still difficult to solve the lower waterproof problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the purpose is to provide an inter-block coupling structure of a prefabricated rainwater storage tank that does not require (thus) filling work grooves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the present invention is another object to provide a block structure of the wall block, the index plate and the prefabricated rainwater storage tank to effectively prevent the leakage of stored rain while (thus) combining the wall block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101282720-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the present invention provides a long-term supply of the water required for landscape water while (thus) effectively storing rainwater flowing down by heavy rain on an inclined surface, and also to perform long-term landscaping by wicking the stored rainwater for the storage tank of the stacked blocks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, the excellent connection pipe 400 for supplying the rainwater from the rainwater receive (thus)r 100 to the filtration tank 300 includes a communication hole (not shown) on one side of the rainwater receiver 100, and may be connected to the connection port of the filtration tank 300 through the ground under the sidewalk block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the present invention can be applied to a storage tank 500 having different water collecting paths different from each other through a rainwater receive (thus)r on the road through which the excellent water quality infiltrated through the water permeable sidewalk block 200 and the relatively contaminated road run- it is possible to store"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receive (thus)r on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518433-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the conventional rainwater storage tank as described above, since the rainwater storage tank is constructed by assembling the storage blocks successively, it is difficult to assemble the storage block if the accuracy of the storage block is not high and the column 16 formed in the storage block 10 is difficult to assemble into the rainwater storage tank 50 so that the effective storage space is reduce (thus)d"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101564767-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a fourth step of constructing a permeable packing layer on the non-point pollution source-reduce (thus)d prefabricated storage block constructed through the third step, into the reservoir space of the non-point pollution source-reduced prefabricated reservoir block through the permeable packing layer, permeable rainwater storage tank for filtering the rainwater and penetrating through the permeable base layer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101611948-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, in order to adjust the weakly acidic rainwater 3 to be weakly alkaline while (thus) removing the foreign substances contained in the rainwater 3 flowing into the inside of the ph adjusting tank 30, and a block 310 in which the elvan stone powder, the powdered activated carbon, and the powdered lime slurry are mixed in the middle portion of the ph adjusting tank 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101857595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater storage tank is advantageous in that the construction cost can be reduced compared with the conventional art because (thus) the rainwater storage tank joins the blocks and the slab through the screw member"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101857595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the blocks used in the rainwater storage tank are usually manufactured as a separate product to meet the construction site, it is difficult to produce standardized blocks, and in order to use blocks smaller or larger than the manufactured blocks, there is a problem that falls significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102005372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even when the fixed mesh filter 110 is blocked, an appropriate amount of rainwater should be introduced into the float removing tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102046131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulate (thus)d in the initial excellent water tank, rainwater tank and sedimentation tank, thereby ensuring the long-term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of the initial excellent water quality treatment system according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to easily clean the contaminants accumulate (thus)d in the initial excellent water tank, rainwater tank and sedimentation tank, thereby ensuring the long-term security of the initial water and rainwater treatment capacity.1 is a block diagram showing an example of rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102110404-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "these plastic storage tanks have the advantage of being able to construct a sturdy rainwater storage tank at a low cost because (thus) the plastic material, which is a raw material, is cheap, but the space between the plastic blocks must be narrowed to sufficiently withstand the load, making it difficult to secure a worker s path"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "in other words, in the above-described embodiment, the planter block while (thus) dividing the collection pipe 16 connected between the rainwater collection rig 10 and the storage tank 20 into the first collection pipe 17 and the second collection pipe 35 each end is connected to a different vegetation hole 31 buried in the ground at 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "rainwater flowing through the collecting pipe 16 or the first collecting pipe 17 may be directly supplied to the storage tank 20 or may be supplied to the storage tank 20 via (thus) the planter block 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "9, rainwater supplied to the storage tank 20 through the water collection pipe 16 or the second water collection pipe 35 di