level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent (thereby) the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a structure is intended to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the water level of the septic tank 30 reaches the full water level due to (thereby) the continuous inflow of the initial excellent water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to (thereby) the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water level of the treated water tank is measured in real time, and when the water level is out of a certain range, the gate valve is selectively opened and closed to block the flow path of the overflow pipe, thereby increasing the overflow height of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200145021-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is a block diagram of a water purifier to which the water level devia (thereby)tion preventing device of the purified water tank according to the present invention is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328661-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the treated water is stored in the backwash tank and the water level falls below a certain level during non-operating, it falls down due to (thereby) the weight of the stopper 9 to block the flow path of the treated water so that the water in the pump head does not empty"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the water tank level is a high water level, the flow of water is blocked by the float 42 and the pressure valve 43, so that the current of the pump motor increases without being stabilized as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height, the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while (thereby) rising upward according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, when the purified water is filled to the water level set in the purified water storage tank (pressure tank), the automatic shut off valve for the water purification system can automatically block the inflow of raw water to the purified water filter due to (thereby) the pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1, the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention [0001] the present invention relates to a water level elevating device for a water-the present invention relates to a water level elevating device, and more particularly, to a water level elevating device for a water pipe turning method applied to a water turning method bypassing a work section of a sub tank for maintenance or monitoring of a sub tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 increases above a predetermined level, the flow rate controller 110 increases the output of the transfer pump 107 to increase the flow amount of sludge transferred to the cavitation storage tank 120, and the sludge storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 is 100 to 120% of the set water level, since the water level becomes the full water level, four cavitation generators 130 corresponding to four levels can be operated to greatly increase the throughput of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water purifier automatic drainage method of another embodiment of the present invention, the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water, the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time, and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed, drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, checking the water level when the water level is confirmed, and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, after checking the water level, including the drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the water tank, it is possible to automatically adjust the water level to prevent (thereby) the overflow of the refrigerant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, when the water level is confirmed for a predetermined number of times or more, a drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, and a water level checking step of checking the water level when the water level is confirmed as a result, errors due to (thereby) internal factors can be recognized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102391446-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "specifically, the control device 30 may determine whether filter cleaning is necessary by checking whether the water level in the water tank is equal to or greater than a preset threshold value based on the water level detection information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102525037-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile (thereby), the pressure tank 100 may be provided with a water level measurement unit (not shown) and a drainage unit 170 for adjusting the water level, and a water level gauge 180 for checking the water level from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived (increase) from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while (increase) passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently (increase) returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 become (increase)s the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention by installing the filtration device 200 in the position as described above, the contaminants in the water discharged through the drain pipe 120 from the swimming pool to be filtered immediately before passing through the water level control tank (300)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is, if the operating time of the filtration tank is increased, the flow rate of the flow of the rainwater or the flow rate of the treated water is lowered due to (increase) the increase of the amount of contaminants collected in the lcd artificial floating filter media, or the water level of the tank before the rainwater is increased do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while (increase) passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200326076-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently (increase) returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the present embodiment, since the sensing unit 58 that detects the water level of the sewage is installed outside the tank 30, the sensing unit 58 may be prevented from malfunctioning due to (increase) severe contamination of the sensing unit 58"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102434590-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the end part is immersed in the water level of undischarged sewage that always remains in the storage state in the sewage tank, so that the negative effects such as contamination of indoor air due to (increase) odors during the sewage discharge operation can be eliminated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102436761-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the end part is immersed in the water level of undischarged sewage that always remains in the storage state in the sewage tank, so that the negative effects such as contamination of indoor air due to (increase) odors during the sewage discharge operation can be eliminated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, the water level in the production water tank 5 reaches the water level l even after the operation time set to sufficiently remove the corrosion promoting component in the feed water as described above to prevent the deterioration of the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102500623-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "an anti-corrosion coating is applied to the outer periphery of the lower part installed inside the wastewater treatment tank 100 to measure the water level inside the tank and prevent corrosion by the sterilizing solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167943-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to one feature of the automatic water supply device of the present invention, both the discharge valve and the water level valve installed in the water tank are made of plastic and rubber packing to prevent rust or corrosion and to have durability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(f2 f3) accordingly, in the present invention, the amount of water stored in the water tank is automatically adjusted to a level higher than the water level capable of detecting a wind speed (wind load) this is to prevent defects due to wind loads such as overturning and partial crushing of the water tank due to insufficient amount of water stored in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100331066-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by equaling the water level in groups, the concrete capacity of decaying tanks is reduced and the simultaneous treatment efficiency is maximized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 is provided with a transfer pump that operates when the predetermined water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank (200) reaches the minimum water level (h2), the agitating unit (500) is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100314663-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and water level (36) (37) is provided, the electronic safety valve (e) automatically discharged to the outside when abnormal pressure to maintain the set pressure and to prevent (increase) damage and deformation of the tank ( 39) and automatic air discharge valves 34 and 35 are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101383594-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and according to the variable level screen filter according to the present invention, it is possible to support the variable screen unit in connection with the water tank to improve the durability of the equipment, the deformation of the variable screen unit according to the water level is made more quickly to increase the treatment efficiency of sewage it can be effective"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032930-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4, two or more rectangular (40 50 mm) steel reinforcing rods 26 are installed in the partition wall 22 in the vertical direction to prevent deformation due to (increase) the water level difference between the tanks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air input through the horizontal passage (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air introduced through the horizontal channel (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using the control equipment, the water level difference between the upper and the downstream filtration tanks is maintained at 1.0-1.5m, so that the sediment deposited in the upper and the downstream filtration tanks can be gradually discharged during the initial flooding with less floating dust, thereby preventing the ultimate closure of the filter media"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the circuit for detecting the water level in the water receiving tank is a low voltage ac circuit in order to avoid electric shock and prevent (increase) electrolysis because the electrodes are always submerged"}, {"pat_id": "KR