ge end of the valve body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403906-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in such a state, when rainwater flows instantaneously, when the rainwater is instantaneously introduced, the floats 40 are raised to block the inlet 12 of the buoy automatic shutoff valve body 10 due to (drive) the disk 20, and the sewage and rainwater are sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in treating rainwater containing a large amount of turbidity, a blockage due to a large amount of turbidity may occur in the chamber portion 210 of the vortex valve, so that an outflow downstream from the rainwater discharge portion 130 of the manhole body may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the contaminant discharge pipe 17 is not affected (remove) by the drain opening 22 of the vortex 21 by the double opening / closing valve 24, and always removes the coarse contaminant as the sewage pipe 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the intermediate contaminants included in the initial excellent water are temporarily blocked by the double opening / closing valve 24 sealing the drain hole 22 formed at the bottom of the vortex 21, and finally removed from the sewage pipe 4 when opened"}, {"pat_id": "US-12202741-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (remove), the particulates and other contaminants that can be dislodged and removed by backwashing the resin are caused to flow out the top of the tank, through the valve and are discharged to a suitable waste drain through the drain port c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water-leveling protector 10, thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water-stop valve 7 due to rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the machine-learning algorithm can be trained with data provided from the control unit server 104, data provided by the smart water valve 126, and data associated with the security system 148 to predict devices that are leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in response to providing the data from each of the devices in the monitored property 102 to the trained model, the trained model can produce a predicted device that is leaking based on the detection by the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "should the smart water valve produce a detection that water is leaking or the trained model predict a device that is leaking water in the monitored property 102, the control unit server 104 can provide that detection and/or prediction to the client device 122 of the property owner 120"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "similarly, the security system 148 can transmit a command to the smart water valve 126 to move the position of the ball valve 208 to open in response to the trained machine-learning model predicting no device is leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevent (predict)ed from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100420101-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a flow control valve having an integrally coaxially connected valve body capable of lifting up and down is accommodated inside the manhole cylinder, and the float rises due to a rise in the level of the rainwater introduced through the upper rainwater inlet pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100918431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the existing rain gutter backflow prevention device installed in the field is most often the case that the valve part to be closed by rust is open"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water-leveling protector 10, thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water-stop valve 7 due to rain"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5757052-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the auxiliary valve is installed on the outer periphery of the main valve and consists of a water shielding plate and a projecting floating body that floats it, and the outer periphery of the projecting floating body is used to prevent malfunction of the valve opening and closing due to the wave of rain water surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first method is to install water gates, valves, and movable wear to control the discharge amount at the outlet, and open these facilities at normal times to drain the reservoir water, and then close the water gate to settle down after a certain period of time"}]</data>
