  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100647994-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filter member provided at the inlet side of the body to prevent (drive) a large amount of foreign substances from entering the body, a shutoff valve provided inside the body to block the rainwater introduced through the inlet at a predetermined amount"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100647994-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "side of the body (5) to prevent (drive) the inflow of bulky foreign matter 6 and a shutoff valve 7 provided inside the body 5 to shut off the rainwater flowing through the inlet 2 when the water flows in a predetermined amount, and the rainwater blocked by the shutoff valve 7"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100672275-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the general operation of the rainwater toss is usually performed by sliding the valve valve plate 17 to the lower guide block 27 of the torsion housing 1 by the operation of the drive motor 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the connecting valve 42 is a manure to prevent the failure of the device due to (drive) the pinch of the foreign matter caught in the bent portion of the connecting pipe 41 when the role of water purification and water purification is not made smoothly, it is configured to control inflow and block rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when rainwater is introduced through the manhole cover 30 while (drive) the installation is completed as described above, the introduced rainwater is introduced into the odor blocking tube 110, and the rainwater is opened while the elastic valve 115 is opened by the load of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101537963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve 320 blocks the inflow of rainwater when the filter 331 installed in the filter housing 330 is exchanged, thereby facilitating a smooth filter replacement operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101771073-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve 31 rises above the inflow section 21 of the rainwater infiltration pipe 20 to open the inflow section 21 and contrarily to the lower side of the inflow section 21 to close the inflow section 21, the structured inflow part 21 is not closed but the space between the inflow part 21 and the discharge part 22 is blocked to prevent (drive) the rainwater flowing through the inflow part 21 from flowing to the discharge part 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the branch valve 150 through the upper inlet 154 flows into the side through hole 1572 as the blocking member 156 rotates by a predetermined angle in the lateral direction in accordance with the control signal of the controller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment, when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater, the buoyant elevation part 353 descends, the lifting valve plate 352 is lowered to block the lower portion of the vertical pipe 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328170-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to install a larger number of valves in a limited area of the lid to provide a sewage odor blocking device that can lead to the sewage pipe in a faster time when a large amount of sewage or rainwater is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it has been disclosed that the odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver has a long oval structure so that sludge components contained in rainwater or sewage do not accumulate (drive) in the discharge end of the valve body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403906-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in such a state, when rainwater flows instantaneously, when the rainwater is instantaneously introduced, the floats 40 are raised to block the inlet 12 of the buoy automatic shutoff valve body 10 due to (drive) the disk 20, and the sewage and rainwater are sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in treating rainwater containing a large amount of turbidity, a blockage due to a large amount of turbidity may occur in the chamber portion 210 of the vortex valve, so that an outflow downstream from the rainwater discharge portion 130 of the manhole body may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the vacuum setting step and the rainwater inflow checking step according to the opening of the suction valve 121a can be simultaneously performed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6164161-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "furthermore, it is possible to prevent rainwater (including condensation), dust, and the like from accumulating inside the welded portion between the water storage tank 10 and the valve chamber (30, 52) and causing corrosion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water-leveling protector 10, thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water-stop valve 7 due to rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200163545-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the above problems, and prevents foreign matters and rainwater from accumulating around the valve tube, and facilitates the installation and dismantling of the drinking water and prevents freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100420101-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a flow control valve having an integrally coaxially connected valve body capable of lifting up and down is accommodated inside the manhole cylinder, and the float rises due to (therefore) a rise in the level of the rainwater introduced through the upper rainwater inlet pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment, when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater, the buoyant elevation part 353 descends, the lifting valve plate 352 is lowered to block the lower portion of the vertical pipe 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101569048-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is possible to prevent the entry of rainwater into the water-leveling protector 10, thereby providing a special effect of effectively preventing corrosion and rusting of the water-stop valve 7 due to rain"}]</data>
