  <data key="d5">["vaporization", "alloy", "shearing", "present", "panel", "regard", "reaction", "particle", "extraction", "conductivity", "material", "nitrogen", "time", "deposit", "value", "failure", "waste", "part", "freezing", "clogging", "oxidation", "piping", "salt", "design", "cover", "fluid", "stream", "problem", "process", "gas", "residence", "system", "mixture", "liquid", "water", "reactor", "method", "laboratory", "resistance", "condition", "exit", "zone", "hour", "brine", "operating", "layer", "deformation", "liner", "oxygen", "bottom", "appurtenance", "operation", "leak", "surface", "volume", "force", "rate", "treatment", "cost", "answer", "pressure", "sub", "throughput", "event", "step", "cavity", "pocket", "chamber", "example", "air", "blade", "block", "rotation", "corrosion", "vapor", "sludge", "vessel", "amount", "temperature", "room", "slurry", "iron", "solid", "invention", "degree", "steel", "contaminant", "wall", "attack", "phase", "jet", "subchamber", "excess", "conduit", "heater", "member", "hydrolysis", "oxidant", "case"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["have", "leave", "define", "accord", "emit", "offer", "result", "dislodge", "pass along", "enter", "fill", "conduct", "become", "fall", "run", "compose", "obtain", "pressurize", "maintain", "associate", "form", "accumulate", "keep", "require", "receive", "exit", "raise", "heat", "remove", "produce", "necessitate", "comprise", "let", "occur", "remain", "feed", "increase", "oxidize", "cause", "dissolve", "introduce", "scale up", "be", "fabricate", "enrich", "mean", "provide", "achieve", "vaporize", "reach", "create", "weave", "pass"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11738314-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at block 1310, the high-temperature, high-pressure liquid is received into a vessel having one or more walls that define a hollow interior cavity partially filled with water, with an air pocket within the cavity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659347-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the method according to my invention comprises the steps of (a) emitting the water in one or more jets into a vessel maintained under a pressure low enough to let part of that water be vaporized--together with accompanying contaminants--at an ambient temperature, preferably at or below the usual room temperature of about 20 -25 c."}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high operating temperatures and pressures result in extreme corrosion problems as well as requiring expensive thick-walled piping and reaction vessels"}, {"pat_id": "US-8741100-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "while various different high alloys offer answers in regard to corrosion and temperature resistance, the costs of the vessels and the appurtenances fabricated from them are generally quite high"}, {"pat_id": "US-11318396-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the thermal conductivity of the exterior cover, both the interior woven or non-woven panel and the interior surfaces of the pressure vessel are theoretically capable of reaching temperatures in excess of the deformation temperature of 304 stainless steel"}, {"pat_id": "US-5100560-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any case, the rotation of the blade means 60 will cause the blade members 62 to pass along the interior wall 12 of the vessel 10 dislodging any accumulated deposits which then fall into the brine slurry in the subcritical temperature zone 16 in the bottom of the vessel 10 wherein the solids will dissolve in the cold brine fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-5075010-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "lower temperatures may produce freezing and clogging of the vessels, while higher temperatures may cause vaporization of the water, both unwanted for efficient operation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5126048-A", "para_id": "para_15", "text": "lower temperatures may produce freezing and clogging of the vessels, while higher temperatures may cause vaporization of the water, both unwanted for efficient operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197264-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "when the reaction temperature of the secondary reaction vessel 12 becomes 150 degrees c or less, for example, reaction rates, such as hydrolysis, become slow"}, {"pat_id": "US-5591415-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, in conventional hot-wall design, the pressure vessel wall runs at substantially higher temperature and is consequently much more susceptible to corrosive attack and vessel failure in the event a liner leak occurs"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0513186-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "while (thereby) supercritical water oxidation requires a thicker walled vessel due to higher operating pressure, the less dense process stream in supercritical temperature water oxidation necessitates a larger vessel to achieve a comparable residence time"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1661864-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in the method (1) in which the surface oxidation layer is formed in the gas phase, a mixed gas of a nitrogen gas and a small amount of air is introduced into a reaction vessel at a low temperature to oxidize \u03b1-fe present in the surface of the iron particles, thereby obtaining iron composite particles having a surface oxidation layer composed of fe3o4"}, {"pat_id": "US-5100560-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this oxidation method, the waste material is pressurized and fed into a reactor vessel along with compressed oxidant, either oxygen, air or oxygen-enriched air, and maintained therein under supercritical temperature conditions, that is at a temperature above 374 c., and, elevated pressure, to cause rapid oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5106513-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "while supercritical water oxidation requires a thicker walled vessel due to (thereby) higher operating pressure, the less dense process stream in supercritical temperature water oxidation necessitates a larger vessel to achieve a comparable residence time"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after subcritical wet oxidation treatment, the oxidation mixture exits the reactor vessel 20 via (thereby) a conduit 22 and is heated by a heater 24 to supercritical water temperatures, in excess of 374 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5240619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vapor phase in the subcritical wet oxidation reactor vessel 20 exits via (thereby) a conduit 22 and enters a heater 24 which heats the vapor phase to supercritical temperatures, greater than 374 c"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6535392-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, scaling up to a high throughput commercial volume system in a small laboratory system is a problem associated with achieving and maintaining high pressure in a large extraction vessel to provide constant pressure and temperature while maintaining constant throughput raw materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure, temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values to remove the water from the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure, temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values, to remove the water from the sludge"}]</data>
</edge>
