  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the water channel 10 rises due to (remove) rain or the like, the flow rate increases so that the inflow amount of the contaminant 40 increases, so the removal speed of the contaminant 40 should also proceed rapidly in proportion to the inflow of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by automatically controlling the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in several stages according to the water level of the water channel 10, water flows in the water channel 10 so that the contaminants 40 can be quickly removed when the water level suddenly blows in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "according to one form of the invention, it is provided that the incorrect discharges are transferred into the latter due to (thus) a flow gradient between the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this takes advantage of the fact that in a separation system the dirty water channel is always lower than the rain water channel and thus the dirty or waste water in the rain water channel can get into the dirty water channel due to (thus) the natural flow gradient"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if the rainwater channel to the dirty water channel is not closed off, water can thus pass from the rainwater channel to the dirty water channel, but not vice versa"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event of a short-term backwater in the dirty water channel and thus the connection line being closed, the water from the tap can be temporarily stored in dry weather and then drained off"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "because of (thus) the rain water still flowing in small quantities through the rain water channel 2, the dirty water channel 4 experiences a second flush with rain water through the connecting line 5"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to (thus) the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200314265-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by automatically controlling the driving speed of the lifting motor 26 in several stages according to the water level of the water channel 10, water flows in the water channel 10 so that the contaminants 40 can be quickly removed when the water level suddenly blows in rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904287-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the initial excellent water is collected by the installation of the wear member 115, the existing water channel, that is, the water drainage section (back water) due to the reduction of the cross section of the sewage pipe 1 causes an obstacle to the rainwater outflow due to the back water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100904287-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the initial excellent water is collected by the installation of the wear member 115, the existing water channel, that is, the water drainage section (back water) due to the reduction of the cross section of the sewage pipe 1 causes an obstacle to the rainwater outflow due to the back water"}]</data>
